            <ArticleTitle>Hand Pain in a Golfer: A Case Report of a Metacarpal Stress Injury and a Review of the Literature Regarding Return to Play in Grip Athletes.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">1941738116676085</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 19-year-old golfer presented to the sports clinic with a 2-week history of dominant-hand pain after several months of daily golf. He had a metacarpal stress fracture. This case discusses the athlete's return-to-play timeline as well as reviews the current limited literature guiding return to play in grip athletes.</AbstractText>
